@startuml new-op
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans SC"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #6B5FA0
skinparam TitleFontColor #4A2C8F
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #8E6CCF
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #3AA9B8
  DiamondBackgroundColor #E2F6F8
  StartColor #6B5FA0
  EndColor #6B5FA0
}
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #CFC6E6
  TitleFontStyle bold
}
title Adding an op: the developer's steps and the system's checks

|#F8F5FD|Developer|
start
:Write the spec with status spec-only;
|#F3FBFC|System|
:The validator checks the signature
statically and instantiates every
workload row;
|Developer|
:Write the call spec, the kernel interface
and its implementations: override entry_for
where needed, and declare devices,
supported_archs, applies, preferred_over
or general;
:Write the Op class (~__init~__, kernel_types,
interfaces, forward, docstring), and export it
from its package and tileops.<family>;
|System|
:Generate the call checks, shape inference,
dtype checks and eval_roofline from the
signature, and for a compile-boundary class
the operator and fake/meta;
|Developer|
:Write ref_program in workloads/;
:Write correctness tests in tests/ops/:
BUILTIN target by default, device from
run_device(), marked in_tree_kernels
or cuda_only where needed;
:Write the benchmark function in
benchmarks/ops/: cases from bench.cases,
and the implementations to compare,
add a case entry in benchmarks/_cases/;
:Set status to implemented;
|System|
:CI: the validator checks code against
the spec, then manifest tests and
correctness tests on a GPU;
while (Checks pass?) is (no)
  |Developer|
  :Fix the implementation, not the spec;
  |System|
  :CI checks again;
endwhile (yes)
:Merge into main;
:Nightly runs the benchmarks by case id
and checks every call is measured;
:The roofline tool computes efficiency,
and the docs site updates;
stop
@enduml
